assistant: Subject: accept epoch-ms created_at in get_order

The fix doesn't address the 404 in the alert. Vendor version 2026-10-01 now sends `created_at` as epoch milliseconds (e.g. `1792315539045`) instead of an ISO-8601 string. `get_order` ran it through `Date.parse(String(...))`, which gave NaN, so every order on the new version would show 1970-01-01. `get_order` now uses numeric values directly as epoch ms and still parses strings as before. typecheck, lint and tests pass, and the v1 output is unchanged, but no v2 trace exists, so the new path isn't tested. The 404 itself seems to come from the vendor: `create_order` returned exactly what the POST sent back (o-5002, 1499), and nothing in shop-mcp changes what `GET /orders/o-5002` returns. It may be the vendor being slow to make new orders readable, or the new version needing an `Idempotency-Key`. I didn't add one because the replay matches on header names, so it would break the v1 fixtures. The order should stay "unconfirmed" until the vendor side is checked.

